x86_64-linux  there is nothing to compare here, by construction: a case that includes a C++ standard library header is compiled by clang against clang's library, not this one, so the two objects hold the symbols of two different implementations - and on the cross targets clang has no C++ headers and refuses the file outright. Behaviour is the oracle for these, and run.sh asks it on all three machines.
